00:18:01.090 --> 00:18:03.740
Now, one of the first things
that we were going to do

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:06.700
is define exactly what
we want to de-identify.

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:08.860
So to do that, we're going
to navigate back over

00:18:08.860 --> 00:18:13.960
to our security and data
loss prevention in the Cloud

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:14.790
console.

00:18:14.790 --> 00:18:18.240
And we're going to create a
de-identification template.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:19.330
So I click here on create.

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:19.955
Go to template.

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:24.940
We're going to do a
de-identification template.

00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:27.100
Now de-identification
is a term that's

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:29.440
really to a collection
of techniques

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:31.065
to transform this data.

00:18:31.065 --> 00:18:34.600
And in this case, we're going
to do a record transformation.

00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:36.220
And let's just call
this test DID2.

00:18:39.810 --> 00:18:40.560
[INAUDIBLE] here.

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:43.102
Now when we're doing a record
transformation, what that means

00:18:43.102 --> 00:18:45.060
is that we're going to
apply transformations

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:46.920
on an entire column.

00:18:46.920 --> 00:18:49.698
Now we can leverage our info
type inspection as well,

00:18:49.698 --> 00:18:51.990
and that's the thing that we
use to find out the number

00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:53.320
and find that email.

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:55.070
But in this case, we've
already done that.

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:57.930
If you remember, we had a
column called VIN and email

00:18:57.930 --> 00:19:00.340
that had sensitive data in it.

00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:04.170
So we're just going to
create a simple template here

00:19:04.170 --> 00:19:06.300
for the field VIN and email.

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:09.927
We're going to do what's called
a primitive transformation.

00:19:09.927 --> 00:19:12.510
So we're not going to rely on
it finding the email and the VIN

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:14.652
because we already know
that column has it.

00:19:14.652 --> 00:19:16.360
And we're going to
simply go in and we're

00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:20.680
going to do a deterministic
token or shoot optimization.

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:23.710
What that's going to do is
convert the VIN and the email

00:19:23.710 --> 00:19:27.970
into a token that keeps
deterministic and referential

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:29.007
integrity.

00:19:29.007 --> 00:19:31.090
Then I'm going to cancel
this because I've already

00:19:31.090 --> 00:19:34.900
created that template that we're
going to use, which is listed

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:41.330
here as next 2020 CARS DID 1.

00:19:41.330 --> 00:19:45.140
Now I'm going to navigate
over to data flow.

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:47.180
Now, in data flow, we've
actually already got

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:48.140
this pipeline running.

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:49.980
But just to show you
how we got there,

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:52.820
we'll click on Create
Job from template.

00:19:52.820 --> 00:19:53.860
We name our job.

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:57.330
This will be test job 1.

00:19:57.330 --> 00:19:59.300
And we actually pick an
existing template here

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:04.280
called masking tokenization
for Cloud DLP to BigQuery.

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:06.478
This is going to ask us
for a few parameters.

00:20:06.478 --> 00:20:08.270
Again, it wants to know
the path that we're

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:11.090
going to land or drop
our CSV files into,

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:13.675
where do we want to
injest them into BigQuery.

00:20:13.675 --> 00:20:15.800
And again, that reference
to that de-identification

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:18.130
template that we just created.

00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:20.610
So again, filling this
out, clicking run job,

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:22.340
that's how we get
this pipeline started.

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:25.356
Let's actually go and show
